I posted yesterday and received a couple of responses (Thanks to those who did), but my needs have evolved slightly.
I am creating figures for 75 species at nine different park units and may have need to do this several times, so I'm really in need of a method to loop this process to create consistent figures quickly.

The looping itself was quite easy to figure out, however I'm having difficulties creating a title that satisfies three criteria:

a. I need to italicize the species name which is contained within the figure title (i.e.Mean Suitability in Anonymous National Park for Canus lupus by Year)
b. It should be able to wrap to at least two rows so the title is not wider than the figure itself.
c. Since I am looping this, I need to draw the species name to be italicized from the dataset that I am creating the figure from.

